om/users/stuartcarnie/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"author_association":"MEMBER","issue_field_values":[],"type":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"sub_issues_summary":{"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"### Tested versions\n\n- Reproducible since #105884\n\n### System information\n\nGodot v4.5.beta (c0c1b3839) - macOS Unknown (26.0.0) - Multi-window, 1 monitor - OpenGL 3 (Compatibility) - Apple M3 Max - Apple M3 Max (16 threads) - 48.00 GiB memory\n\n### Issue description\n\nUsing [`DisplayServer.screen_get_scale()`](https://docs.godotengine.org/en/stable/classes/class_displayserver.html#class-displayserver-method-screen-get-scale) always return `1`, which is the default `DisplayServer` value, when the player is embedded. It doesn't return this value when it's not (like an exported game or the editor).\n\n### Steps to reproduce\n\n- Call `DisplayServer.screen_get_scale()` in an embedded player context, see that it returns a wrong value (if your screen scale is higher than `1.0`) \n\n### Minimal reproduction project (MRP)\n\n[macos-display-server-screen-get-scale.zip](https://github.com/user-attachments/files/21418587/macos-display-server-screen-get-scale.zip)","closed_by":{"login":"Repiteo","id":17489292,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE3NDg5Mjky","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/17489292?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo","html_url":"https://github.com/Repiteo","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/